In a larger company, Argo CD may run in a separate management AKS cluster and deploy to several other clusters. For our take-home-sized project, running Argo CD in the same AKS cluster is acceptable.

Next we will install it locally first:

Namespace: argocd
Argo CD components: local Docker Desktop cluster
Medical application target: medical-argocd namespace
Source: your GitHub repository

Once this works, moving it to AKS will use nearly the same Application manifest. Only the image repository, credentials, ingress, and Azure-specific configuration will change.


For the actual architecture:

GitHub repository
       ↓
Argo CD running in AKS
       ↓
Helm chart
       ↓
Medical API Pods in AKS
