Next we’ll test a real GitOps deployment:

Change the memory limit in values.yaml.
Commit and push to GitHub.
Argo CD detects the commit.
Argo CD updates the Deployment.
Kubernetes replaces the Pod.
Revert through Git—not helm rollback.

This demonstrates the actual workflow the medical company is likely using.


Force Argo CD to refresh immediately:

kubectl annotate application medical-api `
  -n argocd `
  argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard `
  --overwrite

Watch the GitOps deployment:

kubectl get application medical-api -n argocd -w

In another terminal:

kubectl get pods -n medical-argocd -w

